24/Feb/26 11:45 AM;712020:b2a39849-1f84-43df-9964-f5586bb81e48;*Fix committed* — {{4a32bcc}} on {{main}}

*Root cause:* The filter container wrapping the sort dropdown had {{overflow-hidden}} CSS class. This creates a clipping boundary that hides absolutely-positioned children (the dropdown menu) regardless of their z-index value.

*Fix:* Removed {{overflow-hidden}} from the filter container in {{search-content.tsx:530}}. The sort dropdown (with {{z-[100]}}) now renders above the container as intended.

*File changed:* {{apps/web/src/app/[locale]/(customer)/search/_components/search-content.tsx}}

Ready for retest — deploy needed to verify on production.
